  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Zach Whitman said GSA was among the first agencies to bring technologies such as the internet and email into the federal workplace, and he described AI proliferation as an opportunity to improve access to federal information and services while ensuring government data are accessible to AI systems. He characterized GSA as an enabler for the federal workforce and said a major issue is calculating return on investment for AI. In 2025, he said GSA’s data-driven approach set a precedent and fostered public trust, described building an enterprise-wide platform from equitable data, and said an early internal AI tool would seek staff feedback while upholding safety, quality, and performance standards.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
